Experiment 6
-------------
The aim of this experiment is to compare the performance of the custom CNN with a pretrained ResNet18 model on the cats-versus-dogs classification task

The custom CNN is trained from randomly initialized weights. ResNet18 uses convolutional features pretrained on ImageNet, while its original classification layer is replaced with a new two-class output layer. The pretrained ResNet18 feature-extraction layers are frozen, so only the new final classification layer is trained

Experimental setup
Both models are trained and validated using the same dataset split to ensure a consistent comparison. A fixed random seed of 42 is used to improve reproducibility.
The following conditions are kept consistent:
Training epochs: 10
Batch size: 32
Optimizer: Adam
Learning rate: 0.001
Loss function: cross-entropy loss
Training augmentations: random horizontal flipping, rotation and colour jitter
Dataset split: 80% training and 20% validation

The custom CNN uses 128 × 128 images to remain compatible with its architecture. ResNet18 uses 224 × 224 images, matching the standard input resolution used by the pretrained model.

Training and validation loss and accuracy are recorded after every epoch. The comparison uses the final-epoch results and the highest validation accuracy observed during training.
Metrics
Final training accuracy: Training accuracy after epoch 10.
Final validation accuracy: Validation accuracy after epoch 10.
Final training loss: Average training loss after epoch 10.
Final validation loss: Average validation loss after epoch 10.
Best validation accuracy: Highest validation accuracy observed across all 10 epochs.

